<h1>Delete your Cairn data</h1>
<p class="lede"><strong>Cairn</strong> is developed by <strong>CappyLabs</strong>.
  This page explains how to delete the data associated with your Cairn identity.</p>

<h2>Option 1 — delete it yourself in the app (immediate)</h2>
<div class="card accent">
  <span class="tag">In-app</span>
  <ol>
    <li>Open <strong>Cairn</strong>.</li>
    <li>Tap the menu (⋮) → <strong>Backup &amp; restore</strong>.</li>
    <li>Under <strong>Danger zone</strong>, tap <strong>Delete this identity</strong> and confirm.</li>
  </ol>
  <p class="note mt-12">This <strong>permanently and immediately</strong>
    deletes your identity and all associated data from the server. It cannot be undone.</p>
</div>

<h2>Option 2 — request deletion by email</h2>
<div class="card">
  <span class="tag">Email</span>
  <p>If you can't access the app, email
    <a href="mailto:<%= privacyEmail %>"><%= privacyEmail %></a> with the subject
    <em>"Cairn data deletion"</em>. If you have it, include your device's public key
    (shown in <strong>Backup &amp; restore</strong>) so we can locate your data.
    We complete deletion within <strong>30 days</strong> and confirm by reply.</p>
</div>

<h2>What data is deleted</h2>
<div class="card">
  <p class="note">When your identity is deleted, we permanently remove:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your <strong>device identity</strong> (your public key and display name)</li>
    <li>Your <strong>connections</strong> (the people you paired with)</li>
    <li>Your <strong>shared locations</strong> — which are <strong>end-to-end encrypted</strong> and cannot be read by CappyLabs</li>
    <li>Your <strong>pairing requests</strong> and <strong>presence timestamps</strong> (last-seen)</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="note mt-12">Deletion cascades: removing your identity removes all of the above.</p>
</div>

<h2>What is kept, and for how long</h2>
<div class="card">
  <ul>
    <li>We do <strong>not</strong> retain personal data tied to your identity after deletion.</li>
    <li>Your location content is <strong>end-to-end encrypted at all times</strong> — CappyLabs never has access to it.</li>
    <li>Routine server security logs (which do not contain your location content) may persist for up to <strong>30 days</strong>, then are purged.</li>
    <li>If you self-host your own Cairn server, your data resides only on your server and is removed when you delete your identity there.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<p class="mt-20">Questions: <a href="mailto:<%= privacyEmail %>"><%= privacyEmail %></a></p>
